  "verbalization": "The compound (17S)-9-hydroxy-4,5-dimethoxy-16-oxa-24-azapentacyclo[15.7.1.18,12.02,7.019,24]hexacosa-2,4,6,8,10,12(26)-hexaen-15-one appears to interact with U373 MG through multiple pathways. It is a target of MIP, which in turn targets Maplexin A, and Maplexin A targets U373 MG. Additionally, the compound is a target of Myricetin-3-O-Beta-D-Glucuronide, which also targets U373 MG. These interactions suggest a complex network of targets that ultimately lead to the effect on U373 MG. The evidence points to a potential mechanism involving the activation of downstream targets that influence the behavior of U373 MG, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
